As of 8/27/26 this is the most current version of the airtable script. 

In order to change the analysts names, go to line 20 and the list should be there.

As of right now the way to get the most automated: 
1. Click on the info icon for the top alert. 
2. Go to the JSON tab
3. Ctrl + a > ctrl + c
4. paste into powershell script
Note: The way the link works is it takes your current tab and since being on JSON makes the link longer it autocuts the link at the first question mark

These are the categories that fill every time: 

Stellar #
Who
What
When
Where
Stellar URL
Severity
Escalation Required (Mentor review everytime)
Kill Chain Stage
Source Host
Destination Host (if no destination host is found in the json or case breakdown, it will copy the source IP)
Analyst selection
Supporting notes (have to fill out some parts manually)

These are the categories that work most of the time: 

MITRE Tactic 
1. Will work if the tactic is listed in airtable
2. If the tactic is not listed and the kill chain stage is "Initial Attempts" it will fill in "Initial Access"
3. If none of the above it will be blank

Detection Type
This is made up of if statements 
1. If "Sophos" (not case sensitive) appears anywhere it will be an "EDR alert" this one takes priority over XDR
2. If "XDR" (case sensitve) appears it will be a "SEIM Correlation" 
3. If none of the above it will be blank

JSON of the event
1. The link with most JSONs is too long causing a crash so there is an if statement that will paste it if there is space
Unlike the other two this one doesn't work most of the time

Parts that don't work at all:
Issue
Tenant Name
Description
